<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Copenhagen (1801)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1801">1801</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolutionary-wars">French Revolutionary Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> was fought on 2 April 1801 when a British fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyde-parker">Sir Hyde Parker</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> leading the attack, engaged the Danish-Norwegian fleet moored before Copenhagen. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> struck because <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> had joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-armed-neutrality">League of Armed Neutrality</a>. After hard fighting a truce was agreed, and Denmark left the league. Nelson is said to have ignored a signal to withdraw.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-copenhagen-1801.jpg" alt="Battle of Copenhagen (1801)" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicholas Pocock · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Copenhagen,_2_April_1801_RMG_BHC0529.tiff" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
